ASP Workflow - Button & Lookup Access Summary
Short summary based only on the provided LWC / Apex / Flow logic and screenshots
1. Button Visibility
Note: The conditions below apply after the workflow panel itself is available to the user.
Button	Permission / User Requirement	Record / Work Item Condition
Submit for Approval	User must be the Standard Owner and have the class-specific OWNER permission set.	Status = Draft; Stage = New, Revising, or Revising from Send Back.
Withdraw	User must be the Standard Owner and have the class-specific OWNER permission set.	Status = Draft; Stage = New, Revising, or Revising from Send Back.
Recall	User must be the Standard Owner and have the class-specific OWNER permission set.	Draft + Pending Acknowledgement OR Acknowledged + Pending Approval.
Reassign Approver	User must be the Standard Owner and have the class-specific OWNER permission set.	Draft + Pending Acknowledgement OR Acknowledged + Pending Approval.
Acknowledge	ASP_ACKNOWLEDGER	User has an Assigned Acknowledgement work item; Status = Draft; Stage = Pending Acknowledgement.
Approve	Class-specific APPROVER permission set.	User has an Assigned Approval work item; Status = Acknowledged; Stage = Pending Approval.
Send Back	User qualifies for Acknowledge OR Approve.	Shown in the same Acknowledge / Approve action group.
2. Approver Lookup List
The Flow formula selects the approver permission set from the Standard Class:
Standard Class	Approver Permission Set
Business	ASP_BUS_APPROVER
Data	ASP_DATA_APPROVER
Application	ASP_APP_APPROVER
Technology	ASP_TECH_APPROVER
Important: The screenshot proves the class-to-permission-set mapping. Any additional filters used to build the final user list are not established from that screenshot alone.
3. Acknowledger Lookup List
The “Get Eligible Acknowledgers” Flow gets the Acknowledger Permission Set and then gets Permission Set Assignee records. The permission set shown is ASP_ACKNOWLEDGER.
Therefore, ASP_ACKNOWLEDGER assignment is the proven permission-set basis for the Acknowledger list. Any other filtering beyond the shown Flow elements is not established from the provided screenshot.
Class-specific OWNER permission sets used by the buttons: Business = ASP_BUS_OWNER; Data = ASP_DATA_OWNER; Application = ASP_APP_OWNER; Technology = ASP_TECH_OWNER.
